  "certified": 0,
  "notice": "A starting point, not certified for the country. Check each column against the instrument before you rely on it. Art. 22(3) lists the register's data, lettered; each column is headed by its letter. Item (a), the drug's scientific name, form, strength and size, heads each page: put them in the item's name. Item (b), the previous balance, is worked out by the register for each entry. The ID number is read from the customer's record (the counter-rules app's national or residence ID): the buyer's, so sell to the patient's own customer record. The patient's age is worked out from the date of birth on that record, at the entry's date; the medical file prints empty: write it in. Item (g) is for warehouses only. The book's period is six months, from 1 January and 1 July, for the statement of Art. 16(2), whose data are this register's own; Art. 16 names neither a start nor a due day, so the reminder falls on the period's last day. The statement's signatures and seal (Art. 16(1)) and the yearly close (Art. 22(5)) are not printed: sign and seal the printed pages. The pharmacy's prescriptions register (Art. 21(2), kept 5 years) lists no fields and is not set up.",
  "sources": [
    "Executive Regulation of the Narcotics and Psychotropic Substances Control Law, Council of Ministers Resolution 201 of 10/6/1431H: Arts. 16, 21, 22 (Bureau of Experts text, as archived 2026-02-09)"
  ],
